cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the report, please cite it as below."
title: "Count Each Idea Once: Building Robust Composites from Correlated Alpha Signals"
authors:
  - family-names: Almodamagha
    given-names: Hashim
    affiliation: "Master of Financial Engineering, UC Berkeley Haas School of Business"
date-released: 2026-07-25
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/HashimAlmodamagha/ultramarin-feature-composition"
abstract: >-
  A Berkeley MFE industry project sponsored by Ultramarin. On four anonymized feature
  classes, composition methods from equal weighting through supervised regressions, PLS,
  gradient-boosted trees, redundancy-aware clustering and a random-effects estimator borrowed
  from clinical meta-analysis are evaluated under one fixed framework (daily rank IC with
  Newey-West significance, signal decay, factor turnover, purged cross-validation) and a
  final frozen test on a blind hold-out. The selected methodology clusters near-duplicate
  variants into blocks, averages within blocks, weights the blocks equally, adds learned
  per-feature transforms only where in-sample evidence supports them, and freezes every
  parameter.
keywords:
  - quantitative finance
  - alpha signals
  - feature composition
  - information coefficient
  - meta-analysis
